 "business": {
  "status": "ok",
  "overview": [
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 37,
    "excerpt": "Havells India Limited is a leading Fast Moving Electrical & Electronic Durables (FMED) Company with a presence in over 70 countries. It offers a diversified range of products spanning across 24 product verticals and 6 brands - Havells, Lloyd, Havells Crabtree, Standard, REO and Havells Studio. The product portfolio covers a gamut of household, commercial and industrial electrical needs.",
    "section": "Corporate overview"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 170,
    "excerpt": "Introduction & Background 1.1 About Havells India Limited Havells India Limited is a leading Indian multinational diversified Fast Moving Electrical Goods (FMEG) and consumer durables Company having presence in more than 70 countries worldwide, manufacturing a wide range of electrical products for residential, commercial and industrial use.",
    "section": "Board's report"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 44,
    "excerpt": "During the year, to further strengthen our position in this space, we made a strategic investment in Goldi Solar, one of India’s leading solar panel manufacturers. This partnership ensures stable and quality supply of solar panels,",
    "section": "Leadership message"
   }
  ],
  "segments": null,
  "management": [
   {
    "sourceId": "call-2026-10",
    "page": 11,
    "excerpt": "If you look at to the underground cable business, few things. One, we've maintained that we were a bit delayed in terms of capex, which we have caught up in the last couple of years. And this is a business where there is huge opportunity for growth as well, with newer customer segments opening up.",
    "speaker": "Anil Rai Gupta"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "call-2026-10",
    "page": 4,
    "excerpt": "So, you know, there is not much of quarter one, I would say, spillover because, as you would realize, that our major business comes from residential switchgear, which is not really order input-based in terms of long-term orders. This is primarily a lot of B2C sales through the channel network. We do believe that, overall, there is a very good, positive growth over the first 6 months.",
    "speaker": "Anil Rai Gupta"
   }
  ]
 },
